# Write your commit subject above these comments, then add a blank line and
# an optional body explaining why the change is needed.
#
# Recommended subject: type(scope)!: description
# Allowed types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci,
# chore, revert.
# Scope and ! are optional. Use ! for a breaking change and explain it.
# Use exactly one space after the colon and a nonblank, single-line description.
#
# Examples:
# docs: improve Android setup
# fix(daemon): correct pairing expiry message
# feat(pwa)!: change machine pairing flow
#
# Local commit messages are recommendations, not enforced by a hook.
# The PR title is checked on GitHub and becomes the squash commit subject.
# All template lines are comments; Git's normal cleanup ignores unused guidance.
